 "name": "Os Esquilos: night look",
 "notes": "Clean light (Esme 2026-11-17: no hazy clouds): solid pixels only, no dithering. Outside: every day colour name -> its night colour from the Rio map's night palette v2 (LK.night_of); each lamp, lantern and candle gets a tight solid halo of v2 glow twins (1-2 steps) and at most a small solid patch beneath; the open doors, paper lanterns and candles use v2 night lights (nl_*). Inside: the room in a warm, colourful dusk ('inside_dusk': cream plaster to deep rose-plum, never lilac or grey), with tight solid halos of lamplight ('inside_lamp' core, 'inside_lamp_edge' halo and patch) at each wall lamp, candle and the stove fire; the windows show the night forest (night twins). No new day colours.",
